<% content_for :title, 'Course Plot' %>

<%= render 'help/page', title: 'Course Plot' do %>
  <div class='space-y-8'>

    <p class='text-fg-muted'>
      Plots a jump route between two star systems using the same pathfinding the referee's ship
      would follow, honouring jump range, fuel availability, and any excluded travel zones. See
      <cite>Core Rulebook, p. 157</cite> for the jump mechanics this planner models.
    </p>

    <div>
      <dl class='space-y-6'>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>From / To</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Origin and destination star systems, chosen by search. When opened from a star system
            or stellar object's show page, From defaults to that system — this can still be
            changed.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Ship</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Optional. Selecting a ship fills in its jump drive rating and manoeuvre drive rating
            as the Jump Range and M-Drive below. Changing either field manually clears the ship
            selection.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Jump Range</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            The maximum jump-<span class='font-mono'>N</span> the ship can make in a single hop
            (1–6). No hop in the plotted route will exceed this distance.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>M-Drive</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            The ship's manoeuvre drive rating, used to estimate in-system transit time to and from
            the jump point at each hop.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Refuelling</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Restricts which systems may be used as refuelling stops along the route:
          </dd>
          <dl class='mt-2 space-y-2 pl-4'>
            <div>
              <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Any</dt>
              <dd class='mt-1'>No fuel restriction — commercial, wilderness, and refined sources all qualify.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>No wilderness (D+ starport)</dt>
              <dd class='mt-1'>Only systems with a class D starport or better qualify; wilderness refuelling stops are excluded.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Wilderness only (gas giant)</dt>
              <dd class='mt-1'>Only systems offering wilderness refuelling (gas giant skimming) qualify.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Refined fuel only (A/B starport)</dt>
              <dd class='mt-1'>Only systems with a class A or B starport qualify, guaranteeing refined fuel.</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Exclude Travel Zones</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Travel zones checked here are avoided entirely — no hop in the route will pass through
            a system flagged with an excluded zone.
          </dd>
        </div>

      </dl>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class='text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-highlight mb-4'>Results</p>

      <p class='text-fg-muted mb-4'>
        Plotting the route shows the hop-by-hop path with jump distance, transit time, and
        cumulative elapsed time for each leg, along with totals for the whole journey. If no route
        satisfies the chosen jump range, refuelling, and travel zone constraints, no route is
        found — try a higher jump range or relaxing the other filters.
      </p>

      <dl class='space-y-6'>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Save to map</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Commits the plotted route as a jump route on the starmap, named and coloured as
            entered. The route is created with type <span class='font-mono'>plotted</span>,
            meaning it stores the origin, destination, and filters used, and can be recalculated
            later from the jump route's edit page.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Plan another route</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Starts a new plot from the same origin system, carrying forward the jump range,
            refuelling, M-Drive, and travel zone exclusions just used.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class='pt-2 text-right uppercase font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.22em] text-fg-muted'>
      REFERENCE 0723RP
    </div>

  </div>
<% end %>